Description
The claimLower() function lacks an expiry mechanism, allowing malicious recipients to indeﬁnitely 
prevent its fund withdrawal when receiving native token. This creates a grieﬁng vector where it’s funds 
remain kept in the contract and in the protocol accounting for as long as the recipient wishes with no 
way for other parties to force execution or reclaim them.
The lower claiming process has two key characteristics that enable this issue:
No expiry validation - Unlike other T2-initiated operations (addAuthor, removeAuthor, publishRoot) which 
include withinCallWindow(expiry) checks, claimLower() has no time restriction:
function claimLower(bytes calldata lowerProof) external whenLowerEnabled lock { 
(address token, uint256 amount, address recipient, uint32 lowerId) =
_extractLowerData(lowerProof);
}
}
